emulator_out.txt
HANDOFF_SESSION_*.md
repomix.config.json

# ─── Graphify knowledge graph ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# graphify-out/ itself is committed (shared map for the whole team); only
# per-machine/per-run local state is excluded.
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root

# ─── UI audit screenshots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Device captures from visual QA runs — ~18MB and regenerated on demand.
# Git history is append-only, so committing binaries this size inflates every
# future clone permanently. Regenerate with the visual-qa skill instead.
screenshots/
# Large regenerable graph artifacts. graph.json is the queryable data and
# graph.html the human viewer — together ~5.4MB. With the post-commit rebuild
# hook active, tracking them would append a fresh 5.4MB blob to history on
# every commit, and git history never shrinks. Rebuilding is local tree-sitter
# parsing with no API cost, so each machine builds its own.
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/*/
graphify-out/*.sig
graphify-out/manifest.json

# ...but DO track the work memory. The graph is regenerable in ~50s of local
# tree-sitter parsing with no API cost; these are not. They are accumulated
# answers that cost real tokens to produce, and `graphify reflect` distills them
# into LESSONS.md (preferred sources / known dead ends / corrections) that every
# future session reads for ~250 tokens instead of re-deriving. Small markdown,
# no blob churn. Commit them so the knowledge survives a clone and reaches
# Antigravity too.
!graphify-out/memory/
!graphify-out/memory/**
!graphify-out/reflections/
!graphify-out/reflections/**

# Sentry Config File
sentry.properties
